1
00:00:00,470 --> 00:00:18,700
Hello, everyone, and welcome back to Real Business English Conversations.

2
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:25,430
We're so happy you joined us today to practice professional English in a natural and realistic way.

3
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:26,200
Hi, everyone.

4
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:28,160
Thanks for being here with us again.

5
00:00:28,220 --> 00:00:34,470
Today, we have another useful office conversation that will help you sound more confident at work.

6
00:00:34,870 --> 00:00:35,370
That's right.

7
00:00:35,770 --> 00:00:40,390
Today's topic is real business English conversations in 80 minutes.

8
00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:51,910
We're going to follow a team through a long and busy work session filled with meetings, planning, problem solving, deadlines, teamwork, and casual office conversations.

9
00:00:51,890 --> 00:01:17,680
you'll hear practical English phrases that people actually use in offices every single day so whether you work in an office now or hope to work in one in the future this lesson is perfect for you alright everyone let's begin today's conversation good morning everyone thanks for joining today's strategy meeting morning Claire looks like the whole team is here already perfect since we have a lot to discuss today

10
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,380
Let's get started immediately.

11
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:20,300
Sounds good.

12
00:01:20,740 --> 00:01:23,200
Should I share the updated agenda on the screen?

13
00:01:23,630 --> 00:01:24,450
Yes, please.

14
00:01:24,830 --> 00:01:26,610
That'll help everyone follow along.

15
00:01:27,130 --> 00:01:27,610
All right.

16
00:01:28,070 --> 00:01:31,220
The first topic is the Client Expansion Project.

17
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:32,000
Great.

18
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:34,620
Daniel, could you give us a quick update?

19
00:01:35,090 --> 00:01:35,330
Sure.

20
00:01:35,370 --> 00:01:40,330
The project is progressing steadily, but we've encountered a few unexpected delays.

21
00:01:40,830 --> 00:01:43,040
What kind of delays are we talking about?

22
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:46,290
Mainly technical issues with the client's database system.

23
00:01:46,670 --> 00:01:49,770
Their software isn't fully compatible with our platform yet.

24
00:01:50,290 --> 00:01:50,720
I see.

25
00:01:50,780 --> 00:01:53,420
Has the IT department found a solution?

26
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:58,210
They're working on it now, but it may take another week to fully resolve the issue.

27
00:01:58,390 --> 00:01:58,970
Hmm.

28
00:01:59,470 --> 00:02:01,400
Will this affect the final launch date?

29
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:02,480
Possibly.

30
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:06,830
If the problem continues, we may need to extend the timeline slightly.

31
00:02:07,270 --> 00:02:07,750
All right.

32
00:02:08,210 --> 00:02:12,540
Please keep us updated because the client is expecting regular progress reports.

33
00:02:13,020 --> 00:02:13,380
Of course.

34
00:02:13,910 --> 00:02:15,750
I'll send another update this afternoon.

35
00:02:16,310 --> 00:02:16,990
Excellent.

36
00:02:17,070 --> 00:02:18,780
Now, let's move on to marketing.

37
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:22,000
Sophia, how is the advertising campaign going?

38
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:23,490
Overall, pretty well.

39
00:02:23,910 --> 00:02:27,690
The social media engagement numbers have improved significantly this month.

40
00:02:28,090 --> 00:02:28,890
That's good news.

41
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:29,900
What changed?

42
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:34,880
We started focusing more on short video content and customer success stories.

43
00:02:35,430 --> 00:02:36,110
Interesting.

44
00:02:36,550 --> 00:02:38,590
And people are responding positively?

45
00:02:38,570 --> 00:02:38,970
Yes.

46
00:02:39,490 --> 00:02:44,880
Our audience seems to prefer authentic and simple content instead of highly polished advertisements.

47
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:47,060
Honestly, I'm not surprised.

48
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:50,120
People trust real experiences more these days.

49
00:02:50,620 --> 00:02:51,080
Exactly.

50
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:55,010
We also collaborated with a few industry influencers last week.

51
00:02:55,450 --> 00:02:57,010
Did that help increase traffic?

52
00:02:57,370 --> 00:02:57,910
Definitely.

53
00:02:58,330 --> 00:03:02,370
Website visits increased by almost 30% in just four days.

54
00:03:02,870 --> 00:03:04,290
Wow, that's impressive.

55
00:03:04,740 --> 00:03:05,120
Thank you.

56
00:03:05,510 --> 00:03:07,400
The team worked really hard on it.

57
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:08,500
Great job, everyone.

58
00:03:08,820 --> 00:03:11,460
It's nice to see strong results after all that effort.

59
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:12,410
Thanks, Claire.

60
00:03:12,710 --> 00:03:14,790
We're happy the campaign is performing well.

61
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:15,710
All right.

62
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:16,710
Next topic.

63
00:03:17,150 --> 00:03:20,260
We need to discuss customer complaints from the past quarter.

64
00:03:20,740 --> 00:03:23,000
I reviewed the support tickets yesterday evening.

65
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:24,860
What patterns did you notice?

66
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:31,390
Most complaints were related to delayed email responses and technical confusion during account setup.

67
00:03:31,370 --> 00:03:32,580
That's concerning.

68
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,280
How long are customers waiting for replies?

69
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:38,130
Sometimes up to two business days.

70
00:03:38,630 --> 00:03:40,250
That's definitely too long.

71
00:03:40,750 --> 00:03:41,220
I agree.

72
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:43,980
The support team has been overloaded recently.

73
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:46,430
Should we hire additional staff?

74
00:03:46,410 --> 00:03:49,710
Either that or improve the automated support system.

75
00:03:50,070 --> 00:03:50,740
Good point.

76
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:56,430
Automation could reduce simple questions and allow employees to focus on more complicated issues.

77
00:03:56,950 --> 00:03:57,410
Exactly.

78
00:03:57,870 --> 00:04:00,530
We could also add tutorial videos to the website.

79
00:04:00,970 --> 00:04:01,890
I like that idea.

80
00:04:02,380 --> 00:04:06,020
Visual instructions are often easier for customers to understand.

81
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,660
Especially for new users who aren't familiar with the platform yet.

82
00:04:10,150 --> 00:04:10,630
All right.

83
00:04:10,990 --> 00:04:15,050
Let's develop a proposal for both ideas and compare the costs.

84
00:04:15,070 --> 00:04:15,510
Sounds good.

85
00:04:15,950 --> 00:04:17,860
I'll work on that with the support department.

86
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:18,700
Perfect.

87
00:04:19,100 --> 00:04:24,360
By the way, before we continue, could we quickly discuss the conference schedule for next month?

88
00:04:24,780 --> 00:04:25,280
Of course.

89
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:26,140
What's the issue?

90
00:04:26,610 --> 00:04:31,130
Some employees are worried about overlapping presentations and travel times.

91
00:04:31,260 --> 00:04:34,130
Ah, I noticed that too when reviewing the calendar.

92
00:04:34,570 --> 00:04:38,770
A few team members might miss important sessions if the timing stays the same.

93
00:04:38,790 --> 00:04:41,890
Then we definitely need to reorganize the schedule.

94
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:43,600
I was thinking the same thing.

95
00:04:44,060 --> 00:04:46,640
Maybe we should split the team into smaller groups.

96
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:47,700
That could work.

97
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:51,650
One group could focus on networking while the other attends workshops.

98
00:04:52,150 --> 00:04:52,810
Exactly.

99
00:04:52,850 --> 00:04:56,930
That way we maximize productivity without exhausting everyone.

100
00:04:56,910 --> 00:04:57,530
Good idea.

101
00:04:57,570 --> 00:04:59,820
I'll update the schedule later today.

102
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:00,600
Thank you.

103
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:01,520
No problem.

104
00:05:01,930 --> 00:05:02,750
All right, everyone.

105
00:05:03,070 --> 00:05:06,960
Let's take a quick 10-minute coffee break before moving to financial planning.

106
00:05:07,420 --> 00:05:08,100
Sounds perfect.

107
00:05:08,620 --> 00:05:10,690
I really need caffeine right now.

108
00:05:10,780 --> 00:05:12,110
Honestly, same here.

109
00:05:12,170 --> 00:05:14,290
This morning has already been hectic.

110
00:05:14,670 --> 00:05:15,650
Welcome back, everyone.

111
00:05:16,010 --> 00:05:16,710
Let's continue.

112
00:05:17,130 --> 00:05:17,550
All right.

113
00:05:18,030 --> 00:05:20,440
Now we need to discuss the quarterly budget.

114
00:05:20,940 --> 00:05:22,960
I prepared the expense report this morning.

115
00:05:23,340 --> 00:05:23,660
Great.

116
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,840
Could you walk us through the major numbers?

117
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:26,600
Sure.

118
00:05:27,290 --> 00:05:31,190
Overall, spending increased by 12% compared to last quarter.

119
00:05:31,570 --> 00:05:33,030
That's higher than expected.

120
00:05:33,430 --> 00:05:34,740
What caused the increase?

121
00:05:35,260 --> 00:05:40,300
Mostly travel expenses, software upgrades, and external consulting fees.

122
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:40,980
I see.

123
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,590
Do you think these expenses were necessary?

124
00:05:43,610 --> 00:05:45,310
For the most part, yes.

125
00:05:45,830 --> 00:05:48,820
The software upgrades improved efficiency significantly.

126
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:49,960
That's true.

127
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:53,260
I've already noticed faster reporting speeds myself.

128
00:05:53,790 --> 00:05:54,230
Exactly.

129
00:05:54,710 --> 00:05:58,310
However, I do think we could reduce travel costs moving forward.

130
00:05:58,750 --> 00:06:01,880
Maybe we should replace smaller meetings with video calls.

131
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:04,800
That would definitely save money and time.

132
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:08,970
Plus, fewer business trips can improve work-life balance for employees.

133
00:06:09,430 --> 00:06:09,950
Good point.

134
00:06:10,430 --> 00:06:14,120
Some team members have mentioned feeling exhausted after constant travel.

135
00:06:14,460 --> 00:06:16,080
Burnout is a serious issue.

136
00:06:16,420 --> 00:06:18,620
We need to manage workloads more carefully.

137
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:19,700
Absolutely.

138
00:06:20,150 --> 00:06:22,630
A healthy team is usually a more productive team.

139
00:06:23,070 --> 00:06:24,530
I completely agree with that.

140
00:06:24,990 --> 00:06:27,300
Should we also review overtime policies?

141
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:28,280
Yes.

142
00:06:28,430 --> 00:06:32,630
I think we should encourage managers to monitor employee schedules more closely.

143
00:06:33,050 --> 00:06:36,440
Some departments have been working late almost every night recently.

144
00:06:36,820 --> 00:06:38,660
That's not sustainable long-term.

145
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:39,660
Exactly.

146
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:43,200
People need proper rest to stay motivated and creative.

147
00:06:43,690 --> 00:06:44,080
All right.

148
00:06:44,490 --> 00:06:47,770
Let's include workload management in next week's leadership meeting.

149
00:06:48,150 --> 00:06:48,510
Will do.

150
00:06:48,890 --> 00:06:49,230
Great.

151
00:06:49,710 --> 00:06:53,920
Now, before we continue, does anyone have any questions about the budget report?

152
00:06:54,380 --> 00:06:58,060
I actually have one question regarding software subscriptions.

153
00:06:58,110 --> 00:06:58,610
Go ahead.

154
00:06:59,030 --> 00:07:01,860
Are we still planning to renew all of them next year?

155
00:07:02,340 --> 00:07:03,280
Not necessarily.

156
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:07,050
We're reviewing which tools are actually being used regularly.

157
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:08,090
That makes sense.

158
00:07:08,610 --> 00:07:10,870
Some platforms are rarely opened anymore.

159
00:07:11,350 --> 00:07:11,970
Exactly.

160
00:07:12,230 --> 00:07:14,940
There's no reason to pay for tools nobody uses.

161
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:15,700
True.

162
00:07:16,340 --> 00:07:19,370
Maybe we should conduct a company-wide survey first.

163
00:07:19,790 --> 00:07:20,410
Good idea.

164
00:07:20,470 --> 00:07:23,050
That would help us make smarter decisions.

165
00:07:23,030 --> 00:07:25,960
I can prepare a short survey this afternoon if you want.

166
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:26,820
Perfect.

167
00:07:27,020 --> 00:07:27,440
Thank you.

168
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:28,340
No problem.

169
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:30,000
All right, next topic.

170
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:33,770
We need ideas for improving internal communication.

171
00:07:34,190 --> 00:07:37,490
Honestly, communication has been a little confusing lately.

172
00:07:37,530 --> 00:07:38,490
I agree.

173
00:07:38,550 --> 00:07:41,960
Different departments are using too many separate systems.

174
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:43,160
Exactly.

175
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:49,010
Some teams use email, others use chat apps, and others rely on spreadsheets.

176
00:07:48,990 --> 00:07:52,090
That creates unnecessary confusion and delays.

177
00:07:52,530 --> 00:07:53,150
Definitely.

178
00:07:53,190 --> 00:07:56,380
Sometimes important updates get lost completely.

179
00:07:56,780 --> 00:07:59,640
We need a more centralized communication process.

180
00:08:00,140 --> 00:08:03,890
Maybe one main project management platform for the whole company.

181
00:08:04,290 --> 00:08:05,250
That could help a lot.

182
00:08:05,710 --> 00:08:09,160
Employees would know exactly where to check for updates and deadlines.

183
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:10,340
Exactly.

184
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:13,860
Consistency is very important in growing companies.

185
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:17,430
Should we test a few platforms before making a final decision?

186
00:08:17,870 --> 00:08:19,150
Yes, absolutely.

187
00:08:19,590 --> 00:08:22,380
I don't want to rush into another complicated system.

188
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:23,340
Fair enough.

189
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:26,120
We should involve employees in the decision, too.

190
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:27,000
Agreed.

191
00:08:27,370 --> 00:08:30,410
People are more likely to use systems they helped choose.

192
00:08:30,970 --> 00:08:31,650
Very true.

193
00:08:31,690 --> 00:08:32,610
All right.

194
00:08:33,010 --> 00:08:35,480
Now let's move on to team development and training.

195
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:37,740
I actually wanted to discuss that.

196
00:08:37,820 --> 00:08:38,320
Go ahead.

197
00:08:38,820 --> 00:08:43,490
Several new employees mentioned they still feel uncertain about company procedures.

198
00:08:43,990 --> 00:08:44,430
Really?

199
00:08:44,930 --> 00:08:46,780
Even after orientation training?

200
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:47,480
Yes.

201
00:08:48,060 --> 00:08:53,080
Apparently the onboarding sessions are too fast and contain too much information at once.

202
00:08:54,130 --> 00:08:54,210
Hmm.

203
00:08:54,230 --> 00:08:55,530
That's valuable feedback.

204
00:08:56,030 --> 00:08:59,850
Maybe we should create shorter training sessions spread across several weeks.

205
00:09:00,270 --> 00:09:02,180
That sounds much more manageable.

206
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:05,920
People usually learn better step by step instead of all at once.

207
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:07,560
I completely agree.

208
00:09:08,020 --> 00:09:10,610
We could also assign mentors to new employees.

209
00:09:11,110 --> 00:09:12,470
That's an excellent idea.

210
00:09:12,910 --> 00:09:15,830
Having someone to ask questions can make a huge difference.

211
00:09:16,290 --> 00:09:16,980
Exactly.

212
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:20,260
Starting a new job can feel overwhelming sometimes.

213
00:09:20,760 --> 00:09:23,820
Especially in large companies with complicated systems.

214
00:09:24,330 --> 00:09:24,970
Very true.

215
00:09:25,010 --> 00:09:30,070
By the way, I heard the HR department is planning wellness activities next month.

216
00:09:30,220 --> 00:09:31,100
Yes, they are.

217
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:35,780
I think there's going to be a team lunch, a workshop, and an outdoor activity.

218
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:36,840
That sounds fun.

219
00:09:37,340 --> 00:09:39,990
It'll be nice to relax outside the office for a change.

220
00:09:40,410 --> 00:09:41,030
Definitely.

221
00:09:41,430 --> 00:09:44,600
Team bonding activities can really improve morale.

222
00:09:44,650 --> 00:09:45,210
I agree.

223
00:09:45,250 --> 00:09:49,640
Employees work better together when they actually know each other personally.

224
00:09:50,060 --> 00:09:50,740
Exactly.

225
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:54,330
Strong relationships create stronger teamwork.

226
00:09:54,350 --> 00:09:59,700
Speaking of teamwork, I wanted to thank everyone for helping with last week's emergency project.

227
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:02,440
Oh yes, that situation was stressful.

228
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:07,550
It really was, but everyone stayed calm and worked together professionally.

229
00:10:07,530 --> 00:10:10,880
I was honestly impressed with how quickly the team responded.

230
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:11,820
Same here.

231
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:15,400
People volunteered extra time without even being asked.

232
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:17,520
That kind of dedication is rare.

233
00:10:18,020 --> 00:10:18,620
Absolutely.

234
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:22,070
It reminded me how valuable this team really is.

235
00:10:22,570 --> 00:10:23,150
Well said.

236
00:10:23,190 --> 00:10:24,370
All right, everyone.

237
00:10:24,410 --> 00:10:27,490
We're approaching the end of today's 80-minute session.

238
00:10:27,910 --> 00:10:30,200
Time went by surprisingly fast.

239
00:10:30,180 --> 00:10:30,720
It did.

240
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:34,450
Before we finish, let's quickly review the action items.

241
00:10:34,950 --> 00:10:35,370
All right.

242
00:10:35,750 --> 00:10:40,340
Daniel will continue coordinating with the IT department regarding the database issue.

243
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:41,040
Correct.

244
00:10:41,520 --> 00:10:46,690
Sophia will prepare customer support improvement proposals and update the conference schedule.

245
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:47,380
Right.

246
00:10:47,630 --> 00:10:54,130
We'll also review travel budgets, overtime policies, communication systems, and onboarding improvements.

247
00:10:54,610 --> 00:10:55,090
Exactly.

248
00:10:55,530 --> 00:10:59,560
Plus, the company survey for software usage will be prepared this afternoon.

249
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:00,940
Perfect summary.

250
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:01,620
Thanks.

251
00:11:02,040 --> 00:11:02,380
All right.

252
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:05,110
Does anyone have any final questions before we end?

253
00:11:05,570 --> 00:11:06,210
Just one.

254
00:11:06,650 --> 00:11:08,950
When is the next strategy meeting scheduled?

255
00:11:09,190 --> 00:11:13,200
Hello, everyone, and welcome back to Business English Conversations.

256
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:14,200
Hi, everyone.

257
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:18,950
Thanks for joining us today for another practical English conversation lesson.

258
00:11:19,570 --> 00:11:20,190
I'm Daniel.

259
00:11:20,610 --> 00:11:21,610
And I'm Chloe.

260
00:11:22,070 --> 00:11:27,320
Today, we're going to practice real business English conversations in 80 minutes.

261
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:28,360
That's right.

262
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:41,780
This conversation will take you through a realistic day at the office filled with meetings, teamwork, client communication, deadlines, office discussions, and problem-solving situations.

263
00:11:41,880 --> 00:11:47,350
You'll hear natural English expressions that professionals use every day in real workplaces.

264
00:11:47,970 --> 00:11:57,260
So if you work in an office, want to improve your business English, or prepare for an international workplace, this conversation is perfect for you.

265
00:11:57,740 --> 00:11:58,480
All right, everyone.

266
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:00,340
Let's begin today's story.

267
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:01,540
Good morning, Chloe.

268
00:12:01,850 --> 00:12:02,830
You're here early today.

269
00:12:03,390 --> 00:12:04,150
Morning, Danielle.

270
00:12:04,530 --> 00:12:08,190
Yeah, I wanted extra time to prepare before the client meeting.

271
00:12:08,750 --> 00:12:09,480
Smart decision.

272
00:12:09,760 --> 00:12:11,600
Today looks extremely busy.

273
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:12,540
Definitely.

274
00:12:13,120 --> 00:12:16,360
I checked my calendar this morning and it's completely full.

275
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:17,480
Same here.

276
00:12:17,840 --> 00:12:20,030
I already have six meetings scheduled.

277
00:12:20,630 --> 00:12:21,650
Six meetings?

278
00:12:22,050 --> 00:12:23,330
That sounds exhausting.

279
00:12:23,890 --> 00:12:26,770
It probably will be, but at least most of them are short.

280
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:27,790
That helps.

281
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:31,080
Long meetings can destroy productivity sometimes.

282
00:12:31,640 --> 00:12:32,640
I completely agree.

283
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:36,110
Did you finish the sales presentation for this afternoon?

284
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:36,970
Almost.

285
00:12:37,390 --> 00:12:39,950
I stayed late last night working on the final slides.

286
00:12:40,380 --> 00:12:42,470
Hopefully the client likes the proposal.

287
00:12:42,950 --> 00:12:43,550
I think they will.

288
00:12:44,010 --> 00:12:46,850
We included several new strategies based on their feedback.

289
00:12:47,390 --> 00:12:47,650
Good.

290
00:12:48,050 --> 00:12:51,900
Clients appreciate when companies actually listen to their concerns.

291
00:12:52,460 --> 00:12:53,100
Exactly.

292
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:56,660
By the way, have you spoken with Michael from IT yet?

293
00:12:57,180 --> 00:12:57,660
Not yet.

294
00:12:58,080 --> 00:12:58,300
Why?

295
00:12:58,340 --> 00:13:02,250
Apparently the conference room projector stopped working again.

296
00:13:02,290 --> 00:13:03,710
Seriously?

297
00:13:03,750 --> 00:13:06,930
Right before an important client presentation?

298
00:13:07,510 --> 00:13:08,770
Unfortunately, yes.

299
00:13:09,050 --> 00:13:11,680
That room always has technical issues.

300
00:13:12,260 --> 00:13:12,560
I know.

301
00:13:12,580 --> 00:13:15,540
Hopefully IT can fix it before 10 o'clock.

302
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:18,080
Otherwise, we'll need a backup plan.

303
00:13:18,620 --> 00:13:19,280
Morning, everyone.

304
00:13:19,770 --> 00:13:20,450
Morning, Sarah.

305
00:13:20,930 --> 00:13:22,350
You both look stressed already.

306
00:13:22,890 --> 00:13:26,110
We just found out the conference room projector isn't working.

307
00:13:26,670 --> 00:13:27,050
Again?

308
00:13:27,090 --> 00:13:29,080
That thing breaks every month.

309
00:13:29,680 --> 00:13:30,380
Exactly.

310
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:33,720
I'll call IT right now and see if someone is available.

311
00:13:34,180 --> 00:13:34,560
Thanks.

312
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:35,800
That would really help.

313
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:37,000
No problem.

314
00:13:37,200 --> 00:13:39,330
So, how's your morning going so far?

315
00:13:39,810 --> 00:13:41,110
Pretty hectic, honestly.

316
00:13:41,150 --> 00:13:44,510
I already received 12 emails marked urgent.

317
00:13:45,090 --> 00:13:46,730
Sounds like a normal Monday.

318
00:13:46,750 --> 00:13:48,380
Unfortunately, yes.

319
00:13:48,960 --> 00:13:53,020
Sometimes I feel like everything becomes urgent in office life.

320
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:56,620
That's because people wait until the last minute to ask for help.

321
00:13:57,250 --> 00:13:57,850
Very true.

322
00:13:57,910 --> 00:14:01,950
Oh, by the way, the CEO will attend the client meeting today.

323
00:14:02,630 --> 00:14:03,330
Seriously?

324
00:14:03,370 --> 00:14:05,670
Nobody mentioned that earlier.

325
00:14:05,890 --> 00:14:09,640
Apparently, he wants to personally review the new partnership proposal.

326
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:13,440
Well, now the pressure just increased significantly.

327
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:14,360
Don't worry.

328
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:15,090
We're prepared.

329
00:14:15,750 --> 00:14:16,350
I hope so.

330
00:14:16,710 --> 00:14:17,410
Good morning, team.

331
00:14:17,970 --> 00:14:18,870
Morning, Mr. Carter.

332
00:14:18,910 --> 00:14:23,380
I just wanted to remind everyone that the client meeting begins at 10 sharp.

333
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:24,500
Understood.

334
00:14:24,980 --> 00:14:28,450
Please make sure your reports and presentations are ready before then.

335
00:14:28,970 --> 00:14:30,970
We're finalizing everything now.

336
00:14:31,020 --> 00:14:31,580
Excellent.

337
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:35,740
Also, I'd like us to focus on clear communication during the meeting.

338
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:36,760
Of course.

339
00:14:37,340 --> 00:14:42,370
The client had concerns last quarter about delayed responses and project coordination.

340
00:14:42,950 --> 00:14:45,950
We've improved those areas significantly since then.

341
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:46,690
Good.

342
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:49,860
Then today is our opportunity to rebuild confidence.

343
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:51,020
Absolutely.

344
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:52,260
All right, everyone.

345
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:53,860
Let's head to the conference room.

346
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:55,960
The clients should be here any minute now.

347
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:57,450
Good morning, everyone.

348
00:14:57,490 --> 00:14:59,490
Thank you for meeting with us today.

349
00:14:59,670 --> 00:15:00,810
Thank you for inviting us.

350
00:15:01,090 --> 00:15:03,640
We're excited to discuss the new project proposal.

351
00:15:04,180 --> 00:15:04,660
Wonderful.

352
00:15:05,180 --> 00:15:08,420
Before we begin, would anyone like coffee or water?

353
00:15:08,950 --> 00:15:10,330
Coffee would be great, thank you.

354
00:15:10,850 --> 00:15:11,250
Of course.

355
00:15:11,790 --> 00:15:14,410
All right, let's begin with introductions first.

356
00:15:15,010 --> 00:15:15,430
Certainly.

357
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:19,320
I'm Chloe, project coordinator for the development team.

358
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:21,900
I'm Daniel, from business operations.

359
00:15:22,370 --> 00:15:25,610
I'll be discussing project strategy and timelines today.

360
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:28,350
And I'm Sarah from Financial Planning.

361
00:15:28,850 --> 00:15:31,730
I'll review budget estimates and cost management.

362
00:15:32,290 --> 00:15:32,690
Excellent.

363
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,320
We appreciate the preparation.

364
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:35,260
Thank you.

365
00:15:35,720 --> 00:15:40,490
To start, we reviewed your concerns from your previous project experience.

366
00:15:40,510 --> 00:15:44,330
Yes, communication delays were our biggest issue last time.

367
00:15:44,870 --> 00:15:46,820
We completely understand that concern.

368
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:53,110
Since then, we've introduced weekly progress updates and faster support response systems.

369
00:15:53,610 --> 00:15:54,690
That sounds promising.

370
00:15:54,920 --> 00:16:01,630
We also created a centralized project management platform so all departments can communicate more efficiently.

371
00:16:02,170 --> 00:16:03,110
Excellent improvement.

372
00:16:03,630 --> 00:16:04,070
Thank you.

373
00:16:04,530 --> 00:16:07,400
Could you explain the proposed project timeline?

374
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:08,340
Of course.

375
00:16:08,880 --> 00:16:13,530
The project would be completed in three main phases over six months.

376
00:16:14,090 --> 00:16:15,730
What happens during the first phase?

377
00:16:16,250 --> 00:16:21,160
The first phase focuses on planning, research, and technical preparation.

378
00:16:21,780 --> 00:16:22,900
And after that?

379
00:16:23,100 --> 00:16:26,920
The second phase involves active development and testing.

380
00:16:27,500 --> 00:16:31,630
I assume the final phase focuses on launch and evaluation.

381
00:16:31,650 --> 00:16:32,170
Exactly.

382
00:16:32,690 --> 00:16:34,450
That timeline seems realistic.

383
00:16:35,010 --> 00:16:39,460
We designed it carefully to avoid unnecessary pressure on either team.

384
00:16:40,020 --> 00:16:40,700
Smart approach.

385
00:16:41,260 --> 00:16:45,640
We learned that rushed projects usually create bigger problems later.

386
00:16:46,200 --> 00:16:46,760
Very true.

387
00:16:47,380 --> 00:16:50,850
Sarah, could you explain the financial estimates next?

388
00:16:50,890 --> 00:16:51,410
Certainly.

389
00:16:51,900 --> 00:16:57,230
Based on our analysis, the total project cost would remain within your approved budget range.

390
00:16:57,780 --> 00:16:58,530
That's good news.

391
00:16:59,050 --> 00:17:03,170
We also included contingency funds for unexpected technical issues.

392
00:17:03,820 --> 00:17:04,740
Excellent planning.

393
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:08,840
Too many companies ignore risk management until problems appear.

394
00:17:09,420 --> 00:17:10,010
Exactly.

395
00:17:10,430 --> 00:17:13,730
Prevention is always cheaper than emergency solutions.

396
00:17:14,330 --> 00:17:15,540
I completely agree.

397
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:20,660
One concern we have is staffing availability during peak development periods.

398
00:17:21,160 --> 00:17:22,160
That's understandable.

399
00:17:22,650 --> 00:17:31,180
To address that, we prepared a flexible staffing strategy using both internal teams and temporary specialists if necessary.

400
00:17:31,640 --> 00:17:33,200
That definitely reduces risk.

401
00:17:33,760 --> 00:17:38,490
We wanted to ensure deadlines remain achievable even during busy periods.

402
00:17:39,090 --> 00:17:40,310
Very professional planning.

403
00:17:40,790 --> 00:17:41,190
Thank you.

404
00:17:41,250 --> 00:17:45,560
I have one question regarding communication frequency.

405
00:17:45,790 --> 00:17:46,190
Of course.

406
00:17:46,770 --> 00:17:49,450
How often would progress meetings take place?

407
00:17:50,060 --> 00:17:54,640
Weekly meetings during active development and bi-weekly meetings during quieter phases.

408
00:17:55,120 --> 00:17:56,070
That seems reasonable.

409
00:17:56,630 --> 00:18:01,110
We also provide written progress summaries after every major milestone.

410
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:02,040
Excellent.

411
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:05,000
Clear communication is extremely important for us.

412
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:07,020
We completely understand.

413
00:18:07,530 --> 00:18:08,310
All right, everyone.

414
00:18:08,570 --> 00:18:11,390
Let's take a short 10-minute break before continuing.

415
00:18:11,660 --> 00:18:12,280
Good idea.

416
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:15,920
Wow, that first session actually went better than expected.

417
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:17,910
I was thinking the same thing.

418
00:18:17,950 --> 00:18:20,610
The clients seemed interested and engaged.

419
00:18:21,090 --> 00:18:24,330
Especially when we explained the updated communication systems.

420
00:18:24,860 --> 00:18:27,040
That was definitely their biggest concern.

421
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:29,380
Good thing we prepared detailed examples.

422
00:18:29,940 --> 00:18:32,360
Preparation makes such a difference in meetings.

423
00:18:32,980 --> 00:18:33,690
Absolutely.

424
00:18:34,210 --> 00:18:38,050
By the way, the projector issue still hasn't been fixed completely.

425
00:18:38,590 --> 00:18:39,350
Seriously?

426
00:18:39,590 --> 00:18:44,530
IT managed to reconnect it temporarily, but they said it could fail any time.

427
00:18:44,570 --> 00:18:46,120
That's not reassuring.

428
00:18:46,720 --> 00:18:47,400
Not at all.

429
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:50,180
Let's keep printed copies ready just in case.

430
00:18:50,720 --> 00:18:51,290
Good thinking.

431
00:18:51,770 --> 00:18:53,430
All right, everyone, let's continue.

432
00:18:53,990 --> 00:18:57,250
Before the break, we discussed timelines and budgets.

433
00:18:57,820 --> 00:19:01,700
Now let's review performance expectations and measurable goals.

434
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:02,840
Perfect.

435
00:19:03,010 --> 00:19:10,100
Our primary goal is improving operational efficiency by at least 20% during the first year.

436
00:19:10,660 --> 00:19:11,540
That's ambitious.

437
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:15,060
It is, but our research suggests it's achievable.

438
00:19:15,600 --> 00:19:18,030
What metrics will you use to measure success?

439
00:19:18,570 --> 00:19:24,730
Customer satisfaction, response times, productivity levels, and project completion rates.

440
00:19:25,310 --> 00:19:26,380
Comprehensive approach.

441
00:19:26,950 --> 00:19:30,480
We wanted measurable results instead of vague objectives.

442
00:19:31,060 --> 00:19:32,120
Smart strategy.

443
00:19:32,290 --> 00:19:37,980
Additionally, we recommend monthly evaluation meetings to monitor progress consistently.

444
00:19:38,500 --> 00:19:40,560
That would help identify issues early.

445
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:41,740
Exactly.

446
00:19:41,780 --> 00:19:45,710
Small problems become expensive when ignored too long.

447
00:19:46,330 --> 00:19:46,890
Very true.

448
00:19:47,550 --> 00:19:51,500
Another important focus is employee training during implementation.

449
00:19:51,980 --> 00:19:52,500
Good point.

450
00:19:52,860 --> 00:19:56,720
New systems often fail because employees aren't trained properly.

451
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:57,700
Exactly.

452
00:19:57,720 --> 00:20:02,390
We want every team member comfortable with the new workflow before launch.

453
00:20:03,050 --> 00:20:04,190
I appreciate that approach.

454
00:20:04,710 --> 00:20:05,110
Thank you.

455
00:20:05,850 --> 00:20:09,360
I think your proposal addresses most of our concerns effectively.

456
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:11,180
We're very happy to hear that.

457
00:20:11,780 --> 00:20:17,090
We still need internal approval from senior management, but overall this looks promising.

458
00:20:17,590 --> 00:20:18,390
Excellent.

459
00:20:18,410 --> 00:20:20,770
We should have a final decision within two weeks.

460
00:20:21,270 --> 00:20:21,710
Perfect.

461
00:20:22,130 --> 00:20:26,800
We'll remain available if you need additional information or revisions meanwhile.

462
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:27,300
Great.

463
00:20:27,760 --> 00:20:30,310
Thank you everyone for your time and preparation today.

464
00:20:30,770 --> 00:20:31,230
Thank you.

465
00:20:31,490 --> 00:20:32,950
We appreciate the opportunity.

466
00:20:33,530 --> 00:20:34,650
Finally, over.

467
00:20:35,340 --> 00:20:37,840
That meeting lasted almost two hours.

468
00:20:38,380 --> 00:20:40,180
Honestly, it felt even longer.

469
00:20:40,820 --> 00:20:42,150
At least it was productive.

470
00:20:42,670 --> 00:20:42,910
True.

471
00:20:43,250 --> 00:20:46,030
The clients seemed genuinely interested in moving forward.

472
00:20:46,630 --> 00:20:51,400
I noticed that too, especially during the discussion about performance metrics.

473
00:20:51,620 --> 00:20:52,000
Yeah.

474
00:20:52,260 --> 00:20:55,580
They asked detailed questions, which is usually a positive sign.

475
00:20:56,100 --> 00:20:56,640
Exactly.

476
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:59,180
I'm glad we practiced beforehand yesterday.

477
00:20:59,870 --> 00:21:00,450
Same here.

478
00:21:00,950 --> 00:21:04,490
Preparation saved us several times during difficult questions.

479
00:21:05,030 --> 00:21:05,550
Definitely.

480
00:21:06,130 --> 00:21:07,910
So, what's next on your schedule?

481
00:21:08,390 --> 00:21:09,960
More emails, unfortunately.

482
00:21:10,320 --> 00:21:12,320
Then a department planning meeting at 3.

483
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:13,980
Sounds exhausting.

484
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:15,020
What about you?

485
00:21:15,040 --> 00:21:19,010
I need to finish the meeting summary report before the end of the day.

486
00:21:19,260 --> 00:21:20,220
That's important.

487
00:21:20,640 --> 00:21:22,460
Management will want updates quickly.

488
00:21:23,040 --> 00:21:23,560
Exactly.

489
00:21:24,080 --> 00:21:25,450
Hey guys, nice work today.

490
00:21:25,950 --> 00:21:26,610
Thanks, Sarah.

491
00:21:27,130 --> 00:21:30,090
Seriously, the presentation looked professional and organized.

492
00:21:30,710 --> 00:21:33,180
I'm just happy the clients responded positively.

493
00:21:33,660 --> 00:21:34,640
They definitely did.

494
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:37,840
I think we have a strong chance of winning the contract.

495
00:21:37,860 --> 00:21:39,730
That would be huge for the company.

496
00:21:40,230 --> 00:21:40,910
Absolutely.

497
00:21:41,470 --> 00:21:44,210
By the way, are you joining the team lunch tomorrow?

498
00:21:44,770 --> 00:21:45,490
I think so.

499
00:21:45,860 --> 00:21:46,820
Where are we going?

500
00:21:46,910 --> 00:21:50,540
There's a new Italian restaurant near the office everyone wants to try.

501
00:21:50,580 --> 00:21:51,860
Sounds good already.

502
00:21:52,380 --> 00:21:54,470
Apparently, their pasta is amazing.

503
00:21:55,010 --> 00:21:56,230
Now I'm definitely going.

504
00:21:56,710 --> 00:21:56,970
Good.

505
00:21:57,010 --> 00:22:00,210
After stressful meetings, we deserve good food.

506
00:22:00,760 --> 00:22:01,760
I completely agree.

507
00:22:02,340 --> 00:22:04,100
Well, I should get started on that.

508
00:22:04,300 --> 00:22:08,590
Hello, everyone, and welcome back to our Business English Practice podcast.

509
00:22:08,770 --> 00:22:09,430
Hi, everyone.

510
00:22:09,630 --> 00:22:11,450
We're really happy to have you here again.

511
00:22:11,490 --> 00:22:21,190
Today, we're going to take you inside a real office environment and show you how fluent natural business English conversations actually sound at work.

512
00:22:21,210 --> 00:22:21,670
That's right.

513
00:22:21,950 --> 00:22:30,190
Instead of memorizing isolated phrases, we'll learn through real situations, real responses, and real workplace communication.

514
00:22:30,170 --> 00:22:40,040
So today's topic is a full office workflow day, from morning check-in to meetings, problem solving, teamwork, emails, and end-of-day reporting.

515
00:22:40,420 --> 00:22:41,220
Let's get started.

516
00:22:41,660 --> 00:22:42,420
Good morning, team.

517
00:22:42,660 --> 00:22:44,690
Let's quickly go over today's priorities.

518
00:22:45,210 --> 00:22:45,550
Morning.

519
00:22:45,770 --> 00:22:50,380
I've checked my emails, and the client from the UK is waiting for an update on the proposal.

520
00:22:50,840 --> 00:22:52,580
Okay, that's our top priority.

521
00:22:53,060 --> 00:22:53,520
Anyone else?

522
00:22:54,100 --> 00:22:57,050
I also need clarification on the marketing budget approval.

523
00:22:57,470 --> 00:22:59,330
Finance hasn't responded yet.

524
00:22:59,390 --> 00:22:59,930
Noted.

525
00:23:00,290 --> 00:23:02,140
I'll follow up with finance directly.

526
00:23:02,700 --> 00:23:04,520
Anything urgent from your side, Daniel?

527
00:23:04,980 --> 00:23:09,290
Yes, I'm still finalizing the sales report, but I might need an extension.

528
00:23:09,670 --> 00:23:11,850
I'm missing some data from the analytics team.

529
00:23:12,370 --> 00:23:12,730
All right.

530
00:23:13,170 --> 00:23:14,850
Send a quick follow-up email.

531
00:23:15,330 --> 00:23:18,080
If they don't respond in an hour, I'll escalate it.

532
00:23:18,680 --> 00:23:19,220
Excuse me.

533
00:23:19,280 --> 00:23:20,340
Do you have a moment?

534
00:23:20,660 --> 00:23:23,160
I need some clarification on the client proposal.

535
00:23:23,620 --> 00:23:23,820
Sure.

536
00:23:24,160 --> 00:23:24,530
Go ahead.

537
00:23:24,950 --> 00:23:26,130
What's unclear?

538
00:23:26,260 --> 00:23:30,880
In Section 3, it says Strategic Alignment with Long-Term KPIs.

539
00:23:31,310 --> 00:23:33,030
What exactly should I include there?

540
00:23:33,430 --> 00:23:34,350
Good question.

541
00:23:34,750 --> 00:23:40,540
It means how our solution supports the client's long-term business goals and performance indicators.

542
00:23:41,180 --> 00:23:43,520
So should I include measurable outcomes?

543
00:23:44,080 --> 00:23:44,620
Exactly.

544
00:23:45,100 --> 00:23:50,830
Add expected growth percentages, cost efficiency improvements, and customer retention impact.

545
00:23:50,810 --> 00:23:51,350
Got it.

546
00:23:51,610 --> 00:23:53,190
That makes much more sense now.

547
00:23:53,450 --> 00:23:53,820
Thank you.

548
00:23:54,360 --> 00:23:54,980
No problem.

549
00:23:55,280 --> 00:23:57,100
Always ask if something is unclear.

550
00:23:57,720 --> 00:23:58,200
All right.

551
00:23:58,440 --> 00:23:59,780
Let's move into the meeting room.

552
00:24:00,080 --> 00:24:03,030
We need to discuss the Q3 performance review.

553
00:24:03,590 --> 00:24:07,770
Before we start, should I present the sales data first or the marketing report?

554
00:24:08,350 --> 00:24:09,450
Start with sales.

555
00:24:09,760 --> 00:24:12,180
Then we'll connect it with marketing performance.

556
00:24:12,460 --> 00:24:17,850
Okay, so overall, sales increased by 12% compared to last quarter.

557
00:24:18,250 --> 00:24:21,340
However, we missed our target in the Asia-Pacific region.

558
00:24:21,780 --> 00:24:23,480
Do we know why that happened?

559
00:24:23,920 --> 00:24:28,830
Yes, mainly due to supply chain delays and reduced advertising presence.

560
00:24:28,970 --> 00:24:30,110
That's important.

561
00:24:30,310 --> 00:24:32,930
We should address both issues in our action plan.

562
00:24:33,490 --> 00:24:34,540
Let's open the floor.

563
00:24:34,820 --> 00:24:38,630
Does anyone have suggestions for improving performance next quarter?

564
00:24:39,190 --> 00:24:44,260
I think we should increase digital marketing spending, especially on social media campaigns.

565
00:24:44,240 --> 00:24:45,660
That's a valid point.

566
00:24:46,100 --> 00:24:48,380
Any objections or alternative ideas?

567
00:24:49,010 --> 00:24:53,310
I agree, but we also need better coordination between sales and logistics.

568
00:24:53,750 --> 00:24:56,860
Otherwise, we'll keep losing clients due to delivery delays.

569
00:24:57,360 --> 00:24:58,320
Good observation.

570
00:24:58,680 --> 00:25:00,870
Coordination is often underestimated.

571
00:25:00,880 --> 00:25:03,850
We'll include that in the improvement strategy.

572
00:25:03,830 --> 00:25:07,170
I'd like to bring up an issue regarding workload distribution.

573
00:25:07,650 --> 00:25:08,040
Go ahead.

574
00:25:08,600 --> 00:25:13,600
Some team members are consistently working overtime while others have lighter workloads.

575
00:25:14,240 --> 00:25:15,340
I've noticed that too.

576
00:25:15,720 --> 00:25:16,640
What do you suggest?

577
00:25:17,310 --> 00:25:23,090
Maybe we can redistribute tasks more evenly or bring in temporary support during peak periods.

578
00:25:23,570 --> 00:25:24,670
That sounds reasonable.

579
00:25:25,080 --> 00:25:28,080
Let's review each department's workload after this meeting.

580
00:25:28,640 --> 00:25:31,700
Now, let's talk about the client email from earlier.

581
00:25:32,160 --> 00:25:33,460
Did anyone reply?

582
00:25:33,550 --> 00:25:34,810
Yes, they responded.

583
00:25:35,130 --> 00:25:38,550
They are concerned about pricing and want a revised quotation.

584
00:25:38,590 --> 00:25:39,430
Okay.

585
00:25:39,860 --> 00:25:41,020
How should we respond?

586
00:25:41,580 --> 00:25:46,970
We should first acknowledge their concern, then explain the value behind our pricing structure.

587
00:25:47,410 --> 00:25:47,710
Good.

588
00:25:48,150 --> 00:25:51,250
Make sure the tone is professional but reassuring.

589
00:25:51,230 --> 00:25:52,530
I'll draft the email.

590
00:25:52,870 --> 00:25:53,760
How does this sound?

591
00:25:54,190 --> 00:25:55,520
Thank you for your feedback.

592
00:25:55,780 --> 00:25:58,300
We appreciate your concerns regarding pricing.

593
00:25:58,760 --> 00:25:59,660
That's a good start.

594
00:26:00,100 --> 00:26:05,450
You can also add, we would like to highlight the additional value included in our premium package.

595
00:26:05,950 --> 00:26:06,470
Perfect.

596
00:26:06,710 --> 00:26:07,490
I'll include that.

597
00:26:07,950 --> 00:26:10,990
Before lunch, let's quickly check project deadlines.

598
00:26:11,440 --> 00:26:12,500
Are we on track?

599
00:26:12,480 --> 00:26:16,320
Mostly yes, but the design team is slightly behind schedule.

600
00:26:16,740 --> 00:26:17,920
What's causing the delay?

601
00:26:18,410 --> 00:26:21,550
They are waiting for final approval on the branding guidelines.

602
00:26:22,150 --> 00:26:24,740
I'll speak with the creative director right after this.

603
00:26:25,540 --> 00:26:28,120
Speaking of lunch, are you joining the team today?

604
00:26:28,660 --> 00:26:29,100
I might.

605
00:26:29,300 --> 00:26:29,980
What's the plan?

606
00:26:30,440 --> 00:26:32,650
We're going to the new cafe downstairs.

607
00:26:33,030 --> 00:26:35,950
They apparently have great business lunch sets.

608
00:26:35,930 --> 00:26:36,690
Sounds good.

609
00:26:37,080 --> 00:26:38,580
I could use a short break anyway.

610
00:26:39,100 --> 00:26:42,590
During lunch, I wanted to ask you something about career development.

611
00:26:43,110 --> 00:26:43,350
Sure.

612
00:26:43,370 --> 00:26:44,410
What's on your mind?

613
00:26:44,930 --> 00:26:47,070
I want to improve my presentation skills.

614
00:26:47,230 --> 00:26:48,180
Do you have any advice?

615
00:26:48,740 --> 00:26:49,060
Yes.

616
00:26:49,620 --> 00:26:52,640
First, focus on structuring your message clearly.

617
00:26:52,930 --> 00:26:54,990
Beginning, middle, and conclusion.

618
00:26:55,490 --> 00:26:58,940
Second, practice speaking slowly and confidently.

619
00:26:59,000 --> 00:27:01,160
I always feel nervous when presenting.

620
00:27:01,610 --> 00:27:02,350
That's normal.

621
00:27:02,570 --> 00:27:03,810
The key is preparation.

622
00:27:04,210 --> 00:27:07,270
If you know your content well, confidence will follow.

623
00:27:07,890 --> 00:27:11,080
After lunch, I need to send a follow-up email to the supplier.

624
00:27:11,520 --> 00:27:12,020
What happened?

625
00:27:12,480 --> 00:27:14,780
They haven't confirmed delivery timelines yet.

626
00:27:15,240 --> 00:27:17,390
In your email, be firm but polite.

627
00:27:17,770 --> 00:27:22,490
You can say, we would appreciate an urgent update regarding delivery schedules.

628
00:27:22,580 --> 00:27:23,100
Got it.

629
00:27:23,360 --> 00:27:24,340
I'll send it right away.

630
00:27:24,860 --> 00:27:27,520
Let's reconvene for a quick afternoon check-in.

631
00:27:27,820 --> 00:27:28,370
Any updates?

632
00:27:28,920 --> 00:27:29,210
Yes.

633
00:27:29,430 --> 00:27:32,450
The finance team approved the revised budget.

634
00:27:32,470 --> 00:27:33,050
Great news.

635
00:27:33,670 --> 00:27:35,320
Also, the supplier responded.

636
00:27:35,580 --> 00:27:37,760
They confirmed delivery for next Wednesday.

637
00:27:37,820 --> 00:27:38,760
Excellent.

638
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:40,240
That keeps us on track.

639
00:27:40,820 --> 00:27:43,570
I also had a short conversation with the new intern.

640
00:27:44,070 --> 00:27:45,110
How is she settling in?

641
00:27:45,690 --> 00:27:49,600
She's doing well, but she's a bit unsure about company procedures.

642
00:27:49,580 --> 00:27:52,520
Let's assign someone to guide her for the first week.

643
00:27:53,020 --> 00:27:53,600
Good idea.

644
00:27:53,960 --> 00:27:55,780
I'll help her with onboarding documents.

645
00:27:56,220 --> 00:27:59,930
Before we wrap up the day, let's review key tasks.

646
00:27:59,950 --> 00:28:00,250
Sure.

647
00:28:00,550 --> 00:28:01,270
I'll summarize.

648
00:28:01,670 --> 00:28:07,890
Client proposal updated, finance approved, supplier confirmed, and workload review scheduled.

649
00:28:08,370 --> 00:28:09,280
Perfect summary.

650
00:28:09,890 --> 00:28:10,560
One more thing.

651
00:28:10,940 --> 00:28:13,480
I think we should improve internal communication.

652
00:28:13,880 --> 00:28:15,920
Sometimes updates get delayed.

653
00:28:16,020 --> 00:28:16,880
I agree.

654
00:28:16,940 --> 00:28:20,660
Maybe we should use a shared dashboard for real-time updates.

655
00:28:21,200 --> 00:28:23,870
That would reduce confusion and email overload.

656
00:28:24,370 --> 00:28:26,570
Let's propose it in the next management meeting.

657
00:28:27,110 --> 00:28:29,150
Before we leave, I have a quick question.

658
00:28:29,610 --> 00:28:33,020
How do you usually handle difficult conversations with clients?

659
00:28:33,680 --> 00:28:35,140
I focus on three things.

660
00:28:35,560 --> 00:28:40,850
Stay calm, listen carefully, and respond with solutions rather than problems.

661
00:28:41,110 --> 00:28:41,950
That makes sense.

662
00:28:42,390 --> 00:28:46,660
So instead of saying, we can't do it, we say, here's what we can do.

663
00:28:47,260 --> 00:28:47,760
Exactly.

664
00:28:48,020 --> 00:28:49,820
It keeps the conversation productive.

665
00:28:50,380 --> 00:28:54,170
I think I'm starting to understand how real business communication works.

666
00:28:54,630 --> 00:28:56,850
It's not just English, it's strategy.

667
00:28:57,270 --> 00:28:57,750
That's right.

668
00:28:58,230 --> 00:29:02,060
Business English is about clarity, confidence, and collaboration.

669
00:29:02,600 --> 00:29:05,560
And also being polite but direct at the same time.

670
00:29:06,100 --> 00:29:06,660
Exactly.

671
00:29:06,960 --> 00:29:09,680
That balance is what makes communication effective.

672
00:29:09,900 --> 00:29:11,960
All right, I think that wraps up our day.

673
00:29:12,020 --> 00:29:14,230
Yes, great work today, everyone.

674
00:29:14,470 --> 00:29:17,330
Let's continue tomorrow with the next phase of the project.

675
00:29:17,870 --> 00:29:19,150
Thanks for listening, everyone.

676
00:29:19,330 --> 00:29:23,190
We hope this helped you understand real workplace English conversations.

677
00:29:23,760 --> 00:29:24,960
See you in the next episode.

678
00:29:25,340 --> 00:29:26,060
Hello, everyone.

679
00:29:26,380 --> 00:29:28,980
Welcome back to our English practice podcast.

680
00:29:29,440 --> 00:29:31,060
We're so happy you joined us today.

681
00:29:31,100 --> 00:29:32,120
I'm Ryan.

682
00:29:32,570 --> 00:29:33,350
And I'm Olivia.

683
00:29:33,830 --> 00:29:37,410
Today, we're going to practice real office English conversations.

684
00:29:37,610 --> 00:29:38,170
That's right.

685
00:29:38,550 --> 00:29:46,160
These are the kinds of conversations people use in meetings, presentations, project discussions, and everyday business situations.

686
00:29:46,680 --> 00:29:54,030
If you work in an office or plan to work in an international company someday, this lesson will help you speak more naturally and confidently.

687
00:29:54,590 --> 00:29:58,660
So grab your notebook, listen carefully, and repeat the phrases after us.

688
00:29:59,180 --> 00:30:02,930
Today's topic is advanced office meeting English conversations.

689
00:30:03,490 --> 00:30:04,530
Let's get started.

690
00:30:04,590 --> 00:30:05,550
Good morning, everyone.

691
00:30:06,130 --> 00:30:08,160
Thanks for joining the weekly strategy meeting.

692
00:30:08,620 --> 00:30:09,100
Good morning.

693
00:30:09,580 --> 00:30:11,520
I reviewed the agenda earlier this morning.

694
00:30:12,020 --> 00:30:13,780
Looks like we have a lot to discuss today.

695
00:30:14,320 --> 00:30:15,140
Yes, we do.

696
00:30:15,680 --> 00:30:17,610
Especially regarding the new product launch.

697
00:30:18,130 --> 00:30:19,570
I'm excited about that project.

698
00:30:19,790 --> 00:30:22,310
The market response has already been very positive.

699
00:30:22,910 --> 00:30:23,650
Absolutely.

700
00:30:24,110 --> 00:30:26,560
But we still need to finalize the pricing strategy.

701
00:30:27,120 --> 00:30:29,740
Have we received the latest competitor analysis yet?

702
00:30:30,240 --> 00:30:30,500
Yes.

703
00:30:30,840 --> 00:30:33,060
The research team sent it yesterday evening.

704
00:30:33,280 --> 00:30:33,620
Great.

705
00:30:33,940 --> 00:30:35,830
I'd love to review the numbers during the meeting.

706
00:30:36,390 --> 00:30:36,870
Definitely.

707
00:30:37,470 --> 00:30:40,900
Before we begin, let's quickly go over last week's action items.

708
00:30:41,480 --> 00:30:41,760
Sure.

709
00:30:42,100 --> 00:30:45,810
I completed the client follow-up emails and updated the sales projections.

710
00:30:46,470 --> 00:30:46,910
Excellent.

711
00:30:47,390 --> 00:30:48,980
Did the clients respond positively?

712
00:30:49,240 --> 00:30:50,090
Most of them did.

713
00:30:50,110 --> 00:30:54,170
A few clients requested additional information about our subscription plans.

714
00:30:54,670 --> 00:30:55,630
That's understandable.

715
00:30:56,070 --> 00:30:58,220
People always want clear pricing details.

716
00:30:58,780 --> 00:30:59,340
Exactly.

717
00:30:59,400 --> 00:31:00,980
Especially corporate clients.

718
00:31:01,400 --> 00:31:04,590
They usually compare several providers before making a decision.

719
00:31:05,210 --> 00:31:05,830
Very true.

720
00:31:06,490 --> 00:31:07,850
What about the marketing materials?

721
00:31:08,090 --> 00:31:09,550
Were those finalized?

722
00:31:09,570 --> 00:31:09,970
Almost.

723
00:31:10,270 --> 00:31:12,780
The design team is making a few final adjustments.

724
00:31:13,360 --> 00:31:13,600
Good.

725
00:31:14,120 --> 00:31:15,840
I want everything ready by Friday.

726
00:31:16,320 --> 00:31:17,780
We should be on schedule.

727
00:31:17,850 --> 00:31:18,370
Perfect.

728
00:31:18,950 --> 00:31:20,750
Now let's move on to the budget discussion.

729
00:31:21,330 --> 00:31:23,300
I looked at the financial report this morning.

730
00:31:23,620 --> 00:31:26,080
Some departments exceeded their monthly spending limits.

731
00:31:26,660 --> 00:31:28,100
Yes, I noticed that too.

732
00:31:28,620 --> 00:31:30,830
Travel expenses increased significantly.

733
00:31:31,430 --> 00:31:34,150
Mostly because of the international conference last month.

734
00:31:34,690 --> 00:31:35,190
Right.

735
00:31:35,730 --> 00:31:38,520
But the conference generated several strong business leads.

736
00:31:39,060 --> 00:31:39,660
That's true.

737
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:44,230
Sometimes higher expenses are justified if they create long-term opportunities.

738
00:31:44,480 --> 00:31:45,820
I agree completely.

739
00:31:46,320 --> 00:31:48,500
Did we already calculate the return on investment?

740
00:31:48,980 --> 00:31:51,230
Not yet, but the finance team is working on it.

741
00:31:51,650 --> 00:31:51,890
Good.

742
00:31:52,370 --> 00:31:54,010
We'll need those numbers for the board meeting.

743
00:31:54,590 --> 00:31:57,840
Speaking of the board meeting, are you presenting the quarterly results?

744
00:31:58,320 --> 00:32:00,800
Yes, and honestly, I'm a little nervous.

745
00:32:01,300 --> 00:32:01,580
Really?

746
00:32:01,620 --> 00:32:04,090
You've presented to the board many times before.

747
00:32:04,790 --> 00:32:07,910
I know, but this quarter was particularly challenging.

748
00:32:08,370 --> 00:32:09,150
That makes sense.

749
00:32:09,430 --> 00:32:11,500
The market has been unpredictable lately.

750
00:32:11,640 --> 00:32:12,510
Exactly.

751
00:32:12,910 --> 00:32:15,510
Customer behavior changed a lot over the last few months.

752
00:32:16,030 --> 00:32:17,990
Especially online purchasing habits.

753
00:32:18,550 --> 00:32:18,870
Yes.

754
00:32:19,290 --> 00:32:21,000
People are spending more carefully now.

755
00:32:21,540 --> 00:32:23,940
Do you think the economy will improve next quarter?

756
00:32:24,520 --> 00:32:28,140
It's hard to say, but analysts seem cautiously optimistic.

757
00:32:28,660 --> 00:32:30,330
Hopefully things stabilize soon.

758
00:32:30,750 --> 00:32:33,430
Businesses perform better when customers feel confident.

759
00:32:33,950 --> 00:32:34,630
Absolutely.

760
00:32:35,150 --> 00:32:36,990
Confidence affects spending decisions.

761
00:32:37,310 --> 00:32:41,320
Speaking of confidence, your presentation skills have improved a lot recently.

762
00:32:41,860 --> 00:32:42,220
Thanks.

763
00:32:42,580 --> 00:32:43,520
I've been practicing more.

764
00:32:44,020 --> 00:32:44,580
It shows.

765
00:32:44,920 --> 00:32:47,290
You sound much more relaxed during meetings now.

766
00:32:47,850 --> 00:32:50,590
I used to get extremely nervous before presentations.

767
00:32:51,190 --> 00:32:51,510
Really?

768
00:32:51,530 --> 00:32:53,000
You never seemed nervous.

769
00:32:53,500 --> 00:32:54,920
Trust me, I was.

770
00:32:55,480 --> 00:32:57,220
Especially during large conferences.

771
00:32:57,720 --> 00:32:59,890
Public speaking can definitely be stressful.

772
00:33:00,390 --> 00:33:01,710
The key is preparation.

773
00:33:02,250 --> 00:33:04,860
The more prepared you are, the more confident you feel.

774
00:33:05,090 --> 00:33:06,210
I completely agree.

775
00:33:06,630 --> 00:33:09,310
I always rehearse important presentations several times.

776
00:33:09,930 --> 00:33:10,560
Same here.

777
00:33:11,130 --> 00:33:13,260
I even practice answering difficult questions.

778
00:33:13,760 --> 00:33:14,400
That's smart.

779
00:33:14,720 --> 00:33:18,180
Unexpected questions can completely change the atmosphere of a meeting.

780
00:33:18,660 --> 00:33:19,380
Exactly.

781
00:33:19,870 --> 00:33:21,670
That's why flexibility is important.

782
00:33:22,310 --> 00:33:25,630
Speaking of flexibility, how's the remote work policy going?

783
00:33:26,170 --> 00:33:27,300
Overall, pretty well.

784
00:33:27,820 --> 00:33:30,000
Most employees appreciate the hybrid schedule.

785
00:33:30,440 --> 00:33:31,400
I can understand why.

786
00:33:31,440 --> 00:33:33,860
Working from home saves commuting time.

787
00:33:33,910 --> 00:33:34,550
Definitely.

788
00:33:35,050 --> 00:33:38,100
But some managers still prefer face-to-face communication.

789
00:33:38,580 --> 00:33:39,660
That's understandable, too.

790
00:33:40,040 --> 00:33:42,040
Certain discussions are easier in person.

791
00:33:42,600 --> 00:33:44,280
Especially brainstorming sessions.

792
00:33:44,860 --> 00:33:45,520
Absolutely.

793
00:33:46,020 --> 00:33:49,570
Creative discussions feel more natural when everyone is in the same room.

794
00:33:50,370 --> 00:33:50,870
I agree.

795
00:33:51,350 --> 00:33:53,770
Video calls are useful, but they're not perfect.

796
00:33:54,230 --> 00:33:54,530
True.

797
00:33:54,930 --> 00:33:58,100
Sometimes technical problems interrupt important conversations.

798
00:33:58,700 --> 00:34:02,480
Speaking of technical problems, did the IT team resolve the server issue?

799
00:34:02,700 --> 00:34:06,380
Yes, apparently the server crashed because of a software update.

800
00:34:06,930 --> 00:34:08,490
That must have been frustrating.

801
00:34:09,030 --> 00:34:09,450
It was.

802
00:34:09,790 --> 00:34:12,680
Several employees couldn't access their files for hours.

803
00:34:13,160 --> 00:34:14,200
That's never good.

804
00:34:14,620 --> 00:34:16,100
Did it affect any client projects?

805
00:34:16,780 --> 00:34:19,200
Fortunately, no major projects were delayed.

806
00:34:19,620 --> 00:34:20,370
That's a relief.

807
00:34:20,870 --> 00:34:23,130
The IT department handled the situation quickly.

808
00:34:23,590 --> 00:34:23,830
Good.

809
00:34:24,330 --> 00:34:26,360
Quick problem solving is essential in business.

810
00:34:26,840 --> 00:34:29,600
Definitely, especially when clients are involved.

811
00:34:29,770 --> 00:34:32,730
Speaking of clients, have you heard from the London account recently?

812
00:34:33,210 --> 00:34:35,770
Yes, they're interested in expanding the partnership.

813
00:34:36,270 --> 00:34:36,690
Really?

814
00:34:36,730 --> 00:34:37,830
That's excellent news.

815
00:34:38,350 --> 00:34:40,620
They were impressed with our recent campaign results.

816
00:34:41,040 --> 00:34:43,200
That campaign performed better than expected.

817
00:34:43,760 --> 00:34:46,260
Social media engagement increased dramatically.

818
00:34:46,300 --> 00:34:47,680
I saw the numbers.

819
00:34:48,040 --> 00:34:50,000
The marketing team did an amazing job.

820
00:34:50,570 --> 00:34:51,140
Absolutely.

821
00:34:51,430 --> 00:34:53,110
Their creativity really stood out.

822
00:34:53,590 --> 00:34:55,810
We should recognize their effort during the company meeting.

823
00:34:56,250 --> 00:34:56,730
Good idea.

824
00:34:57,130 --> 00:34:59,350
Employee recognition improves motivation.

825
00:34:59,690 --> 00:35:00,410
Very true.

826
00:35:01,010 --> 00:35:02,350
People want to feel appreciated.

827
00:35:02,830 --> 00:35:03,310
Exactly.

828
00:35:03,330 --> 00:35:06,050
A little recognition can make a huge difference.

829
00:35:06,610 --> 00:35:10,160
Speaking of motivation, how's your team handling the workload lately?

830
00:35:10,640 --> 00:35:13,040
Honestly, everyone's been extremely busy.

831
00:35:13,080 --> 00:35:14,380
Same here.

832
00:35:14,920 --> 00:35:16,910
This quarter feels more intense than usual.

833
00:35:17,370 --> 00:35:17,910
Definitely.

834
00:35:18,270 --> 00:35:20,590
We've had multiple deadlines at the same time.

835
00:35:21,110 --> 00:35:22,790
That can create a lot of stress.

836
00:35:23,350 --> 00:35:25,900
It does, but the team has stayed professional.

837
00:35:26,030 --> 00:35:26,910
That's good to hear.

838
00:35:27,530 --> 00:35:30,730
Communication becomes even more important during stressful periods.

839
00:35:31,310 --> 00:35:31,890
Absolutely.

840
00:35:32,200 --> 00:35:35,500
Without communication, small problems become bigger problems.

841
00:35:36,040 --> 00:35:36,720
Exactly.

842
00:35:37,140 --> 00:35:38,800
That's why regular check-ins matter.

843
00:35:39,340 --> 00:35:42,030
I started holding shorter daily meetings with my team.

844
00:35:42,490 --> 00:35:43,010
Has it helped?

845
00:35:43,510 --> 00:35:43,970
A lot.

846
00:35:44,370 --> 00:35:46,210
Everyone stays informed and aligned.

847
00:35:46,650 --> 00:35:47,170
That's smart.

848
00:35:47,830 --> 00:35:50,540
Sometimes short meetings are more effective than long ones.

849
00:35:51,060 --> 00:35:52,040
I completely agree.

850
00:35:52,380 --> 00:35:54,920
People lose focus during endless meetings.

851
00:35:55,220 --> 00:35:55,920
Very true.

852
00:35:56,420 --> 00:35:58,750
Nobody enjoys sitting in meetings for three hours.

853
00:35:59,310 --> 00:36:01,090
Especially on Friday afternoons.

854
00:36:01,710 --> 00:36:02,390
Exactly.

855
00:36:02,670 --> 00:36:04,960
At that point, everyone's already thinking about the weekend.

856
00:36:05,500 --> 00:36:07,560
Speaking of weekends, do you have any plans?

857
00:36:08,120 --> 00:36:10,530
I'm planning to relax and spend time with my family.

858
00:36:10,830 --> 00:36:11,290
How about you?

859
00:36:11,310 --> 00:36:13,850
I might go hiking if the weather is nice.

860
00:36:14,310 --> 00:36:15,390
That sounds refreshing.

861
00:36:15,930 --> 00:36:18,400
Sometimes we all need a break from screens and emails.

862
00:36:19,020 --> 00:36:19,740
Absolutely.

863
00:36:20,100 --> 00:36:22,440
Constant notifications can be exhausting.

864
00:36:22,860 --> 00:36:23,560
Very true.

865
00:36:24,080 --> 00:36:26,630
Work-life balance is becoming more important nowadays.

866
00:36:27,190 --> 00:36:27,730
Definitely.

867
00:36:28,130 --> 00:36:30,490
Employees are paying more attention to mental health.

868
00:36:31,110 --> 00:36:33,090
And companies are starting to recognize that.

869
00:36:33,650 --> 00:36:34,680
Slowly but surely.

870
00:36:35,240 --> 00:36:35,920
Exactly.

871
00:36:36,340 --> 00:36:38,660
Healthy employees are more productive employees.

872
00:36:39,280 --> 00:36:44,160
Speaking of productivity, I wanted to ask your opinion about the new project management software.

873
00:36:44,650 --> 00:36:47,690
Honestly, I think it's much better than the old system.

874
00:36:47,940 --> 00:36:48,280
Really?

875
00:36:48,320 --> 00:36:49,800
I'm still getting used to it.

876
00:36:49,820 --> 00:36:50,960
That's normal.

877
00:36:51,340 --> 00:36:53,090
New systems always take time to learn.

878
00:36:53,570 --> 00:36:55,910
True, but the interface feels more modern.

879
00:36:56,330 --> 00:36:58,050
And the reporting features are much stronger.

880
00:36:58,570 --> 00:36:59,550
I noticed that too.

881
00:36:59,610 --> 00:37:02,020
Tracking progress is definitely easier now.

882
00:37:02,540 --> 00:37:03,220
Exactly.

883
00:37:03,680 --> 00:37:05,960
It also improves collaboration between departments.

884
00:37:06,490 --> 00:37:07,210
That's important.

885
00:37:07,530 --> 00:37:09,790
Sometimes departments become too disconnected.

886
00:37:10,450 --> 00:37:10,910
I agree.

887
00:37:11,410 --> 00:37:13,800
Strong communication creates stronger teams.

888
00:37:13,990 --> 00:37:14,740
Absolutely.

889
00:37:15,070 --> 00:37:18,860
That's one reason successful companies focus so much on company culture.

890
00:37:19,280 --> 00:37:20,840
Culture affects everything.

891
00:37:21,280 --> 00:37:25,070
Motivation, teamwork, productivity, and even customer service.

892
00:37:25,590 --> 00:37:26,110
Exactly.

893
00:37:26,450 --> 00:37:28,710
People perform better in positive environments.

894
00:37:29,330 --> 00:37:32,390
Speaking of environments, have you seen the renovated office space?

895
00:37:32,960 --> 00:37:33,240
Yes.

896
00:37:33,560 --> 00:37:34,520
It looks fantastic.

897
00:37:35,060 --> 00:37:37,220
I was surprised by how modern it feels now.

898
00:37:37,700 --> 00:37:40,360
The open workspace definitely makes the office brighter.

899
00:37:40,860 --> 00:37:42,890
And the new meeting rooms are much more comfortable.

900
00:37:43,120 --> 00:37:45,560
I especially like the quiet focus areas.

901
00:37:46,120 --> 00:37:46,680
Same here.

902
00:37:47,070 --> 00:37:48,770
They're perfect for concentrated work.

903
00:37:49,290 --> 00:37:52,190
It's amazing how office design can affect productivity.

904
00:37:52,750 --> 00:37:53,350
Very true.

905
00:37:53,830 --> 00:37:56,120
A comfortable environment helps people focus better.

906
00:37:56,680 --> 00:38:00,180
Speaking of focus, I need to finish preparing tomorrow's proposal.

907
00:38:00,760 --> 00:38:02,670
Is that the proposal for the healthcare client?

908
00:38:03,130 --> 00:38:03,410
Yes.

909
00:38:03,730 --> 00:38:06,350
They requested several changes after our last meeting.

910
00:38:06,870 --> 00:38:09,090
Hopefully the revisions won't take too long.

911
00:38:09,340 --> 00:38:11,030
I think we're almost finished.

912
00:38:11,290 --> 00:38:13,270
We just need final approval from legal.

913
00:38:13,730 --> 00:38:13,970
Good.

914
00:38:14,630 --> 00:38:17,050
Legal reviews always take longer than expected.

915
00:38:17,630 --> 00:38:18,250
Very true.

916
00:38:18,550 --> 00:38:20,110
But accuracy is important.

917
00:38:20,680 --> 00:38:21,400
Absolutely.

918
00:38:21,820 --> 00:38:23,060
Especially with contracts.

919
00:38:23,720 --> 00:38:26,500
One small mistake can create major problems later.

920
00:38:26,980 --> 00:38:27,660
Exactly.

921
00:38:28,160 --> 00:38:31,170
That's why attention to detail matters so much in business.

922
00:38:31,770 --> 00:38:32,730
I completely agree.

923
00:38:32,770 --> 00:38:33,770
All right.

924
00:38:34,270 --> 00:38:37,290
Before we wrap up, let's summarize today's key points.

925
00:38:37,560 --> 00:38:37,920
Sure.

926
00:38:37,980 --> 00:38:41,160
First, the product launch remains on schedule.

927
00:38:41,600 --> 00:38:42,040
Correct.

928
00:38:42,480 --> 00:38:45,050
And the marketing materials should be finalized by Friday.

929
00:38:45,670 --> 00:38:50,230
Second, the finance team will complete the investment analysis before the board meeting.

930
00:38:50,730 --> 00:38:50,990
Right.

931
00:38:51,590 --> 00:38:55,680
And third, we'll continue monitoring employee workload and project deadlines.

932
00:38:56,200 --> 00:38:59,000
We'll also review the hybrid work policy next month.

933
00:38:59,520 --> 00:39:00,180
Exactly.

934
00:39:00,700 --> 00:39:01,160
Anything else?

935
00:39:01,740 --> 00:39:02,020
Yes.

936
00:39:02,300 --> 00:39:06,150
The IT department will provide a full report regarding the server issue.

937
00:39:06,480 --> 00:39:06,980
Perfect.

938
00:39:07,660 --> 00:39:10,830
And finally, we'll prepare additional support for the health care proposal.

939
00:39:11,270 --> 00:39:11,750
Sounds good.

940
00:39:12,170 --> 00:39:13,990
I think today's meeting was very productive.

941
00:39:14,590 --> 00:39:15,030
I agree.

942
00:39:15,070 --> 00:39:18,350
Thank you, everyone, for your hard work and participation.

943
00:39:18,890 --> 00:39:20,090
Thanks for leading the discussion.

944
00:39:20,640 --> 00:39:21,200
My pleasure.

945
00:39:21,700 --> 00:39:24,120
Before we leave, does anyone have any final questions?

946
00:39:24,720 --> 00:39:25,280
Just one.

947
00:39:25,640 --> 00:39:27,980
Should we schedule a follow-up meeting next Wednesday?

948
00:39:28,480 --> 00:39:28,760
Yes.

949
00:39:29,080 --> 00:39:30,550
Wednesday afternoon should work well.

950
00:39:30,990 --> 00:39:31,320
Perfect.

951
00:39:31,590 --> 00:39:33,650
I'll send the calendar invitations after lunch.

952
00:39:34,230 --> 00:39:34,670
Excellent.

953
00:39:34,990 --> 00:39:35,330
Thank you.

954
00:39:35,790 --> 00:39:36,490
No problem.

955
00:39:36,660 --> 00:39:37,540
All right, everyone.

956
00:39:37,800 --> 00:39:38,840
Enjoy the rest of your day.

957
00:39:39,300 --> 00:39:39,640
You too.

958
00:39:39,880 --> 00:39:40,440
See you tomorrow.

959
00:39:40,860 --> 00:39:41,140
See ya.

960
00:39:41,620 --> 00:39:44,680
Hey, before you go, are you joining us for coffee downstairs?

961
00:39:45,320 --> 00:39:45,860
Definitely.

962
00:39:46,310 --> 00:39:48,390
I could use a coffee break after all these meetings.

963
00:39:48,950 --> 00:39:49,490
Same here.

964
00:39:49,730 --> 00:39:51,010
Today's been nonstop.

965
00:39:51,430 --> 00:39:52,290
That's business life.

966
00:39:52,750 --> 00:39:53,410
Always busy.

967
00:39:53,950 --> 00:39:54,590
Very true.

968
00:39:54,890 --> 00:39:56,320
But at least we're making progress.

969
00:39:56,960 --> 00:39:57,580
Exactly.

970
00:39:57,960 --> 00:39:59,600
And progress is what matters most.

971
00:40:00,140 --> 00:40:00,460
All right.

972
00:40:00,680 --> 00:40:03,090
Let's head downstairs before the cafe gets crowded.

973
00:40:03,590 --> 00:40:04,050
Good idea.

974
00:40:04,350 --> 00:40:04,770
Lead the way.

975
00:40:05,270 --> 00:40:06,090
Right behind you.

976
00:40:06,370 --> 00:40:10,540
Hello, everyone, and welcome back to our English conversation practice session.

977
00:40:10,980 --> 00:40:11,400
I'm Chris.

978
00:40:11,860 --> 00:40:12,620
And I'm Emma.

979
00:40:13,150 --> 00:40:16,050
We're really happy you're here learning English with us today.

980
00:40:16,610 --> 00:40:24,450
If you want to improve your English for work, meetings, presentations, and professional communication, today's lesson is perfect for you.

981
00:40:24,680 --> 00:40:25,260
That's right.

982
00:40:25,740 --> 00:40:30,030
Today's topic is real business English conversations in 80 minutes.

983
00:40:30,550 --> 00:40:36,750
We're going to practice natural office conversations that professionals use every day in real business situations.

984
00:40:37,270 --> 00:40:46,860
You'll hear conversations about meetings, deadlines, presentations, teamwork, office problems, project planning, and communication with coworkers and managers.

985
00:40:47,460 --> 00:40:52,650
And just like always, we'll use natural and practical English that you can actually use at work.

986
00:40:52,900 --> 00:40:53,600
All right, Chris.

987
00:40:54,020 --> 00:40:54,740
Are you ready to begin?

988
00:40:54,780 --> 00:40:55,780
Absolutely.

989
00:40:56,080 --> 00:40:56,740
Let's get started.

990
00:40:57,840 --> 00:40:58,580
Good morning, Chris.

991
00:40:59,080 --> 00:41:00,100
You look focused today.

992
00:41:00,600 --> 00:41:01,090
Morning, Emma.

993
00:41:01,590 --> 00:41:03,910
Yeah, I've got a big client meeting in about an hour.

994
00:41:04,570 --> 00:41:05,190
Oh, right.

995
00:41:05,490 --> 00:41:07,790
The international client from Singapore, correct?

996
00:41:08,310 --> 00:41:08,930
Exactly.

997
00:41:09,330 --> 00:41:11,880
They want a full update on the software development project.

998
00:41:12,460 --> 00:41:13,300
Sounds important.

999
00:41:13,720 --> 00:41:14,360
Are you prepared?

1000
00:41:14,900 --> 00:41:18,700
Mostly, but I'm still reviewing some financial reports and timelines.

1001
00:41:19,020 --> 00:41:20,000
That's understandable.

1002
00:41:20,520 --> 00:41:23,240
Large meetings always require extra preparation.

1003
00:41:23,780 --> 00:41:26,130
Especially when senior management is attending, too.

1004
00:41:26,710 --> 00:41:29,050
I heard the company director will join the meeting later.

1005
00:41:29,790 --> 00:41:32,010
Yeah, which honestly makes me even more nervous.

1006
00:41:32,670 --> 00:41:33,330
Don't worry.

1007
00:41:33,390 --> 00:41:35,280
You've handled difficult meetings before.

1008
00:41:35,940 --> 00:41:39,980
True, but international clients sometimes ask very detailed questions.

1009
00:41:40,640 --> 00:41:41,880
That's actually a good thing.

1010
00:41:42,260 --> 00:41:44,070
It shows they care about the project.

1011
00:41:44,380 --> 00:41:45,180
I guess you're right.

1012
00:41:45,700 --> 00:41:47,310
Have you finished the presentation slides?

1013
00:41:47,870 --> 00:41:48,230
Almost.

1014
00:41:48,550 --> 00:41:50,270
I'm making a few final adjustments now.

1015
00:41:50,850 --> 00:41:51,350
Let me guess.

1016
00:41:51,830 --> 00:41:53,710
Too much information on one slide?

1017
00:41:54,290 --> 00:41:55,200
Exactly.

1018
00:41:55,220 --> 00:41:56,040
How did you know?

1019
00:41:56,100 --> 00:41:58,180
Because everyone does that.

1020
00:41:59,300 --> 00:41:59,820
Very true.

1021
00:42:00,300 --> 00:42:02,660
The key is keeping things clear and simple.

1022
00:42:03,200 --> 00:42:03,590
Yeah.

1023
00:42:03,810 --> 00:42:06,530
I'm trying to focus more on visuals and less on text.

1024
00:42:07,150 --> 00:42:07,930
Smart decision.

1025
00:42:08,390 --> 00:42:11,110
Clients usually respond better to charts and graphs.

1026
00:42:11,260 --> 00:42:13,130
Especially during long meetings.

1027
00:42:13,430 --> 00:42:15,450
Nobody wants to read giant paragraphs.

1028
00:42:16,010 --> 00:42:16,650
Exactly.

1029
00:42:17,570 --> 00:42:20,230
By the way, could you review my opening statement quickly?

1030
00:42:20,710 --> 00:42:21,070
Of course.

1031
00:42:21,510 --> 00:42:21,880
Go ahead.

1032
00:42:22,880 --> 00:42:26,400
Good morning, everyone, and thank you for joining today's project review meeting.

1033
00:42:26,880 --> 00:42:27,380
Good start.

1034
00:42:27,840 --> 00:42:28,700
Very professional.

1035
00:42:29,120 --> 00:42:29,480
Continue.

1036
00:42:30,360 --> 00:42:35,770
Today, we'll discuss project progress, current challenges, and our implementation plan for the next phase.

1037
00:42:36,040 --> 00:42:38,660
That sounds excellent, clear, and confident.

1038
00:42:39,100 --> 00:42:39,550
You think so?

1039
00:42:40,030 --> 00:42:40,510
Definitely.

1040
00:42:40,910 --> 00:42:42,550
Just slow down a little while speaking.

1041
00:42:43,170 --> 00:42:45,120
Ugh, I do speak too fast when I'm nervous.

1042
00:42:45,680 --> 00:42:58,990
Most people do.
